Core now offers public hooks (worktree branch k190-192, commit 7756f33; spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-25-public-hooks-for-raider-design.md). Raider side, in its own repo:
1. _async_http->do_request (Raider.pm:859 compress_history_f, :1733 raid_f) -> $engine->async_request_f($request). Same Future<HTTP::Response>, 4xx/5xx resolve.
2. _async_http->loop (Raider.pm:1555 inline MCP add, :1911 and :2086 wait self-tool delay_future) -> raider owns a loop: lazy overridable attribute defaulting to IO::Async::Loop->new (process-wide loop, the same one the default Net::Async::HTTP backend uses). CLI already has $self->loop; pass it through. Core promises no loop (k192 choice b). Document: when injecting an _async_http client on a non-default loop, pass that loop to Raider.
3. _langfuse_timestamp (Raider.pm:1718,1763,1821,1858,1925,1951,1987,2000,2129) -> $engine->langfuse_timestamp.
4. Usage parsing: _extract_prompt_tokens (Raider.pm:831), _langfuse_usage (:1084), Plugin::Trace::_extract_usage (Trace.pm:136) -> Langertha::Usage->from_raw($data) (undef when not reported; input_tokens/output_tokens/total_tokens). Gains Ollama-native counts.
5. Tests mocking _async_http->loop (t/86_raider_self_tools.t:568,759,935; t/87_raider_plugins.t:312) move to the new names.
6. Raise the Langertha floor to the release that ships these hooks.
Private names keep working in core until then.

REVISED after review (k192 now choice a, ADR 0028; commits df106c2, 338c762): core now has $engine->async_loop returning Maybe[loop] (the injected client's loop, the Net::Async::HTTP loop, or undef on the sync fallback or a loop-less client). Raider item 2 becomes: use $engine->async_loop // IO::Async::Loop->new at Raider.pm:1555/1911/2086, NOT a raider-owned singleton default. Under the old plan a foreign-loop backend hung. Additional checklist items: (M4) other reach-ins to migrate or justify: $engine->_plugin_instances (t/87_raider_plugins.t:541-558), $raider->_plugin_instances from Raider/CLI.pm:1102, _plugin_pipeline_tool_call (Raider.pm:1846, raider's own composed Role::PluginHost, defensible), and $engine->_langfuse_batch (t/82_live_raider.t:140). The engine-side calls in tests would break on a core rename. (M6) semantic difference: _extract_prompt_tokens returned undef when usage was present but had no prompt key, while Usage->from_raw returns a Usage with input_tokens == 0. The _last_prompt_tokens guard must treat 0 as not reported (or check > 0). async_request_f: HTTP error statuses resolve on every backend, but a transport failure fails the future on Net::Async::HTTP and resolves as LWP's synthesized 500 on the sync fallback, so keep checking is_success.

